      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Strategy vs Design Pattern",
      "fontSize": 37.10323924082221,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Strategy vs Design Pattern",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "geczppvm2KAmmRa_WVh83",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 608.0591357460626,
      "y": 3625.611544976903,
      "width": 8,
      "height": 25,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bId",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 474395813,
      "version": 3,
      "versionNonce": 1338721643,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785290160241,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "P09hZOyzvMVrA3JQqs1vA",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 167.5179046727543,
      "y": 3253.3857330341957,
      "width": 777.2350969846601,
      "height": 450,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIe",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 2003316101,
      "version": 1502,
      "versionNonce": 223566027,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785291149144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Both provide basically the same advantage and UML Diagram of both are also\nvery similiar. \n\nSo whats the diff between them?\n-> Intention is the main difference between the two.\n\nIn strategy, we can dynamically change the implementations of our algorithms.\nFor example, today my SUV is using a diesel engine but tomorrow we may use a\nelectric engine in it instead. Strategy design pattern gives us this ability.\n\nin Bridge, what we WANT here is that we have High level part (car) and we\nhave low level part (Engine), we want to be able to dynamically add more types\n(add Sedan, Hatchback) and we also want to be able to dynamically add more\ntypes in the low level part (electric engine). Both can interchangeably VARY\n(not use, VARY). So that we can make any permutation. BUT when we make a\npermutation, but once we make a permutation we cant change that afterwards(\npetrol suv cant then be changed to a diesel SUV)\n ",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Both provide basically the same advantage and UML Diagram of both are also very similiar. \n\nSo whats the diff between them?\n-> Intention is the main difference between the two.\n\nIn strategy, we can dynamically change the implementations of our algorithms.\nFor example, today my SUV is using a diesel engine but tomorrow we may use a electric engine in it instead. Strategy design pattern gives us this ability.\n\nin Bridge, what we WANT here is that we have High level part (car) and we have low level part (Engine), we want to be able to dynamically add more types (add Sedan, Hatchback) and we also want to be able to dynamically add more types in the low level part (electric engine). Both can interchangeably VARY (not use, VARY). So that we can make any permutation. BUT when we make a permutation, but once we make a permutation we cant change that afterwards( petrol suv cant then be changed to a diesel SUV)\n ",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
    {
      "id": "c4pMKBhUuqhmETNjl7uM7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1193.3234719277011,
      "y": 3201.2741592550656,
      "width": 733.3591766357423,
      "height": 225,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 0,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "bIf",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1007263627,
      "version": 643,
      "versionNonce": 650358117,
      "isDeleted": true,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1785291149144,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Real World Use cases for Bridge Design Pattern\n\n-> Low level layer of TV and High Level of Remote can vary independently\nand we can mix/match independently\n-> GUI (Textbox, Dropdown, Radio) [abstractions] and OS(Windows, OS\nX, Linux) [implementations] can also vary both independently, we can mix\nand match. Cause all the gui things look a lil different on all the different\nOS, not too much but a lil, this is because each OS has their own\nimplementation of the abstraction.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Real World Use cases for Bridge Design Pattern\n\n-> Low level layer of TV and High Level of Remote can vary independently and we can mix/match independently\n-> GUI (Textbox, Dropdown, Radio) [abstractions] and OS(Windows, OS X, Linux) [implementations] can also vary both independently, we can mix and match. Cause all the gui things look a lil different on all the different OS, not too much but a lil, this is because each OS has their own implementation of the abstraction.",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
