      "updated": 1785299576079,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "State Design Pattern Definition: \n\nAllows an object to alter its behviour\nwhen its internal state changes. The\nobject will appear to change the class\n\n\n\nif we dont use state design patter\nwhere it is required, then we would need\nto use if-else statements everywhere\nwhich would make out code much more\ncomplicated and more redundant as well\n\n\nUse cases:\n\n-> Vending Machine\n-> Document Editor\n    -> Published state\n    -> Archived State\n    -> Deleted State\n-> ATM \n    -> idle state\n    -> Card Accepting State\n    -> Cash Dispensing State",
      "fontSize": 30.071088117379478,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "State Design Pattern Definition: \n\nAllows an object to alter its behviour when its internal state changes. The object will appear to change the class\n\n\n\nif we dont use state design patter where it is required, then we would need to use if-else statements everywhere which would make out code much more complicated and more redundant as well\n\n\nUse cases:\n\n-> Vending Machine\n-> Document Editor\n    -> Published state\n    -> Archived State\n    -> Deleted State\n-> ATM \n    -> idle state\n    -> Card Accepting State\n    -> Cash Dispensing State",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
  ],
